============================================================================
Q4. Pinning the failure boundary
============================================================================
  Hypothesis from Q3: failures track intermediate_size > 4096, not the I/H
  ratio. nki-library's CTE sharding heuristic forces shard_on_inter=True when
  intermediate_size > 4096; we launch single-core (no SPMD grid), so the
  inter-sharding tile math would divide by a zero worker count.

  If true, the fused MLP cannot run single-core at the sizes that matter
  (Qwen3-8B is I=12288), which is a harder blocker than the weight layout.

